From: fexdroid
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/common: add patch-id wildcard fallback for Adreno 840 (KGSL)

Mesa 26.2.3 already carries the upstream A840 entry (chip_id 0xffff44050A31,
upstream commit 6e359817 "freedreno/common: Add A840 and X2-85", Rob Clark,
Qualcomm, MR !38450).  Over KGSL the kernel reports a 32-bit chip id and
dev_id_compare() only matches it against that entry when it is exactly
0x44050A31 (fuse-id wildcard, exact patch id).  Add a second entry with the
0xff patch-id wildcard so other A840 revisions (e.g. the 2-slice SKU, or a
different patch level on Samsung firmware) still bind to the A840 properties
instead of failing with VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER.  Same GPU properties as
the upstream entry; the distinct name shows in VkPhysicalDeviceProperties.

License: MIT (same as Mesa).  Local fexdroid patch, not upstream.
---
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py	2026-09-25 19:54:17.874104330 +0300
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py	2026-09-25 19:54:17.886236357 +0300
@@ -1425,6 +1425,12 @@
 
 add_gpus([
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050A31, name="Adreno (TM) 840"),
+        # KGSL (Android) reports the 32-bit chip id; the proprietary driver on a
+        # Galaxy S26 Ultra reports 0x44050A31, which the entry above already
+        # matches once the fuse-id wildcard is applied.  Keep a patch-id
+        # wildcard fallback for other A840 revisions/SKUs so they are not
+        # rejected as "unsupported" outright (the name makes this visible).
+        GPUId(chip_id=0xffff44050Aff, name="Adreno (TM) 840 (unknown patchid)"),
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A8XX,
         [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen3, a8xx_base, a8xx_gen2,
